---
title: Garlicky Baby Bok Choy (Syun Yeung Chau Siu Pak Choi 蔥油菜心)
description: Fast, vibrant garlicky greens to cut through rich meats. Quick side dish with crispy garlic and sesame oil finish.
prep time: 5 minutes
cook time: 5 minutes
servings: 2
tags:
  - bok choy
  - vegetable
  - quick
  - chinese
  - side
source: https://thewoksoflife.com/bok-choy
cuisine: Chinese
course: Side
---

== Fry Aromatics ==
-- Keeping the garlic crushed rather than minced prevents it from burning at high heat
Heat the #wok{} over high heat with @neutral oil{14%g}. Add the @crushed garlic{5%cloves} and fry for ~{10%seconds}.

== Toss and Steam ==
Add the @halved baby bok choy{600%g} and toss vigorously.
Add the @Shaoxing wine{15%g}, @salt{3%g}, and @sugar{1%g}. Toss again.
If the wok looks very dry, add @water{15%g}, cover with a #lid{} for ~{30%seconds} to allow the steam to finish cooking the thicker stems.

== Finish ==
Remove lid, drizzle with @toasted sesame oil{4%g}, toss once more, and plate.
